The editor's three named readers (fictional, as always) read the seventy's seventeen files and its 55 pages together, 29 of 53 pictures placed. Held to the end: partly, from all three. Could start their own: maybe. Would buy: maybe, at 8 to 15 pounds.

Writer: 03, 04, 06, 11, 16 and 17 hold for all three; 02 and 07 are skimmed by all three. All three would reach the usable part sooner (16, or a page of it, near the front; the team pattern in 3), and two would fold 15 into 16. Best line, for two: "Nobody needs permission to stop. Everybody needs his to start again."

Designer and publisher: the pictures that help all three are the clock with the five steps (page 20), the day by trigger (26), the hold file (37) and running, held, released (41). Missed by all three: the dashboard (11), the first page of rules as a card (14), the checklist as one printable page (54). Too tight for all three: the failures chapter as a wall of paragraphs (39).

Five changes in order in the summary.

